#	Interview Question	What you should be able to explain
1	What is an LLM, and how does it generate an answer?	Tokens → context → transformer → next-token prediction → response
2	What is RAG and why do we need RAG if we already have an LLM?	LLM knowledge vs external/private knowledge, hallucination, up-to-date data
3	Explain the complete RAG pipeline from document upload to final answer.	Document → Parse → Chunk → Embedding → Vector DB → Retrieve → Context → LLM → Answer
4	What are chunks and why do we split documents into chunks?	Context limits, retrieval accuracy, chunk size, overlap
5	How do you decide chunk size and chunk overlap?	500 tokens, 100 overlap as an example; document structure and retrieval quality
6	What is an embedding? How is it different from the original text?	Text → numerical vector; semantic meaning; similarity search
7	What is a vector database and how does similarity search work?	Embeddings, vector storage, cosine/distance search, top-K
8	Why would you use hybrid search instead of only vector search?	Semantic search + keyword search; exact legal terms, names, IDs, etc.
9	How would you improve poor retrieval results in a RAG system?	Chunking, embeddings, metadata filters, hybrid search, reranking, query rewriting
10	What is reranking and why is it useful?	Initial retrieval → reranker → better Top-K context
11	How do metadata filters work in RAG?	document_id, source_type, page, organization, permissions, date, etc.
12	How would you implement access control in a RAG system?	Authorization during retrieval/query, not retrieving everything and filtering afterward
13	How do you prevent hallucinations in a RAG application?	Grounding, strict prompts, citations, confidence/evaluation, "answer only from context"
14	How do you provide citations with an LLM-generated answer?	Keep document/page/chunk metadata → retrieve → pass metadata to LLM → return citations
15	What happens if the vector database returns irrelevant documents?	Detection → threshold/reranking → fallback → "I don't have enough information"
16	What is LangChain and why would you use it?	Components for loaders, splitters, embeddings, retrievers, LLMs, chains
17	What is LangGraph and how is it different from LangChain?	Stateful workflows/agents, nodes, edges, loops, branching, memory
18	How would you reduce LLM/Claude token usage and cost?	Smaller context, Top-K tuning, chunk optimization, summarization, caching, model selection
19	How would you make a RAG system production-ready?	Redis/cache, async ingestion, queues, monitoring, evaluation, rate limiting, security
20	Design a RAG system that handles millions of documents and high concurrent queries.	API → retrieval service → vector DB → cache → queues → workers → scaling → monitoring
